+//
+// One inset per hunk, right above its first line. It shows the removed lines (if any), with the
+// Accept / Discard buttons hovering over the top right of them, always in the same spot (like
+// Copilot's). An extension can't draw over the editor's own text, so the inset of a pure
+// addition is a line of its own with just the buttons.
+//
+// An inset's height is a whole number of editor lines, set when it is created. The webview
+// derives the editor's line height from its own height, and reports back how many lines it
+// really needs (removed lines can wrap), so the inset is recreated at that height.
+//
